<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Predicting bankruptcy is essential because it enables early identification of companies or individuals facing financial distress. This early warning helps banks, investors, and regulatory bodies to minimize losses, reduce financial risks, and take preventive measures such as restructuring debts or improving financial strategies. For businesses, it ensures stability, builds trust with stakeholders, and supports long-term growth. By predicting bankruptcy in advance, organizations can protect both their financial health and the wider economy.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
